Material Symbols
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The icons in internal/app/icons/ are derived from Google's Material Symbols
(Outlined, weight 400, grade 0, optical size 20), used under the Apache License
2.0.

    https://fonts.google.com/icons
    https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

They reached Astral by way of two sibling projects, Atlas Notes and Atlas
Monitor, so that the three applications share one visual language. The sources
are kept unmodified in assets/icons-src/; scripts/import-icons.sh produces the
files that ship, and changes only the following:

  * the filename, prefixed "astral-" and suffixed "-symbolic", so an icon
    cannot collide with the system theme's own and lose to it during lookup;
  * the nominal width and height, from 20px to 16px;
  * the fill colour, from the preview grey the exporter emits to black, which
    is what GTK expects to recolour.

The path data itself is unchanged.

Two icons in that directory are NOT from Material Symbols and were drawn for
Astral, because the vendored set had no equivalent:

  * astral-characters-symbolic.svg
  * astral-stop-symbolic.svg

They are drawn on the same 960-unit grid at the same optical weight so they sit
with the rest, and are covered by Astral's own licence.

